{"text": "MEMORANDUM January 7, 1972\n\nREC'D\nFEI 578\nSANDERS qe\nHughes RAB, Dr. P, L. Aulbach (2)\nMaije Mel J. Fl Nall\nSanford Me. H. G. Garrett\nBrown ~ Mr. D: L. Haverstock\nDomeck Mr. J.P. Markham\n\nMr. J. W. Groome\n\nReference: Mr. R. J. Kinnee's memorandum to Mr. J. E. Edens\ndated December 15, 1971, which concerned Market\nResearch Project 1971-233 (B236-71-3).\n\nAttached please find a Sample Specification Sheet which outlines\nthe samples requested by Mr, Kinnee.\n\nCigarette Sample #728 will be identical to current KOOL 84.\n\nCigarette Sample #748 will be identical to current KOOL 84\nexcept that the add-on level of Turkish will be increased\nfrom 485% to 10%, In order to maintain WTS and PCL at\ntheir\u2019 current inciuded levels, it will be necessary to make\nthe following adjustments:\n\n1, The add-on level of WIS should be increased from 16.6% to 17.4%.\n2, The add-on Level of PCL should be increased from 15% to 15.7%.\n\nThe Factory Sample Group should prepare the blends for both\nsamples and process them up to and including the addition, of\nthe ONS flavoring application, The flavored tobacco should\nbe moisture selected at a target of 13.0% and delivered to the\nResearch Department for menthol application.\n\nThe Research Department will supply ample quantities of selected\ncigarette paper and filter rods necessary for the production of\nthese samples,\n\nThe Research Department will require for their evaluations sixty\n(60) packs taken in triplicate from each sample and twenty (20)\npacks taken from each sample for moisture determinations.\n\nALL expenses incurred in the production of both samples should be\ncharged to B236~71~3.\n\n=n Me 583143883\nK, A. MANECKE/ndk", "words": [{"text": "MEMORANDUM", "x0": 105, "y0": 74, "x1": 265, "y1": 87, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "January", "x0": 472, "y0": 74, "x1": 552, "y1": 87, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "7,", "x0": 538, "y0": 68, "x1": 554, "y1": 92, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1972", "x0": 563, "y0": 73